{"id": "EUVD-2026-102283", "enisaUuid": "15a4236e-ceea-385d-800b-6d7111257db3", "description": "libTiMidity through 0.2.8 contains an out-of-bounds access vulnerability in init_soundfont() in src/sndfont.c that allows attackers to corrupt memory by supplying unvalidated SF2 preset header bank and preset values. Attackers can craft a .sf2 file whose bank or preset indexes past the 128-entry tonebank or drumset arrays, causing heap memory reads, writes, and application crashes.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:57:45", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T19:35:40", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:L/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/libtimidity-soundfont-generator-oper-oob-write", "https://github.com/sezero/libtimidity/blob/a52adf6aee2635e2a16797213a089c2180e67757/src/sndfont.c#L199-L224", "https://github.com/sezero/libtimidity", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/libtimidity-through-0.2.8-out-of-bounds-access-via-soundfont-preset-header"], "aliases": ["GHSA-c4vh-j2xp-73q4", "CVE-2026-111156"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "ad9b7419-08d3-3211-bd7e-a89c16495fb6", "product": {"name": "libtimidity", "vendor": {"name": "sezero"}}, "product_version": "0.2.8 \u22640.2.8"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "e21b6f24-2069-36b9-bcee-054167e4af94", "vendor": {"name": "sezero"}}], "isExploited": false}